id: pm-rust-4ld8
title: Pin pm-rust CI and release tooling to current pm CLI and pm-changelog
description: "CI and Daily Release still use pm CLI 2026.9.17 and pm-changelog 2026.9.16 while 2026.9.26 and 2026.9.25 are published. Align the workflow and operator command, then prove strict merge-driver health with the published CLI without enabling crate publication."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[4]: ci,compatibility,release,toolchain
created_at: "2026-09-26T13:34:49.757Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-26T13:39:17.985Z"
author: codex
acceptance_criteria: "CI installs and invokes exactly @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.9.26; Daily Release invokes pm-changelog 2026.9.25 with pm CLI 2026.9.26; README operator command matches; workflow syntax, strict merge-driver health, Rust release gate and changelog invocation are verified; PM_RELEASE_APPROVED guard remains"
parent: pm-rust-u4al
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-26T13:39:17.985Z",codex,"2026-09-26: Published @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.9.26 and pm-changelog 2026.9.25 are pinned consistently in CI, release workflow, justfile and README. Exact published-CLI strict merge-driver health passed. Full just release-check passed: 292 Rust tests, 100/100/100/100 LLVM lines/functions/regions/branches, clippy, rustdoc, cargo audit, and changelog check. Workflow YAML parsed. Daily Release remains guarded by PM_RELEASE_APPROVED and Cargo publish=false."
